bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    bitbucket_5xx_error_drops_http_status_2026-10-31, 0, Bitbucket 5xx errors omitted the HTTP status. See the linked document.
    confluence_list_ignores_links_next_2026-10-31, 0, Confluence list and search ignored the next link. See the linked document.
    devhub_minio_truncated_body_reported_as_success_2026-10-31, 0, A truncated MinIO GET reported success. See the linked document.
    jira_search_ignores_next_page_token_2026-10-31, 0, Jira Data Center search ignores startAt paging; Cloud is fixed. See the linked document.
    outlook_email_adapter_get_sent_without_auth_2026-10-31, 0, The Outlook Graph adapter sent GETs without auth. See the linked document.
    tcp_accept_timeout_nonblocking_stream_windows_2026-10-31, 0, TCP accept with timeout returns a non-blocking stream on Windows. See the linked document.
    seed_interpreter_opened_view_read_tuple_index_2026_10_31, 0, Tuple index failure after an encrypted open came from a shadowed binding. See the linked document.
    os_crypto_native_failures_2026_10_31, 0, On the pinned Phase 2 producer AES-128 GCM gives wrong output and X25519 returns zeros then segfaults. AES-256 GCM has no native implementation of rt_tls13_aes256_gcm. Phase 1 passes.
    seed_module_name_shadows_match_binding_2026_10_31, 0, Importing std.common.json.value lets the module name win over a binding called value. DevHub and read path sites are renamed. Many other sites remain exposed.
    native_pattern_payload_text_interpolation_2026_10_31, 0, On the pinned producer a text payload bound by an enum pattern printed as a raw integer. Not tested on a rebuilt compiler.
    devhub_spec_windows_shim_not_executed_2026_10_31, 0, The seed resolves bare names only to exe files on Windows, so fake gh and acli never ran and specs could reach real CLIs. Specs now use absolute cmd trampolines. The seed limit remains.
    os_crypto_partial_helper_rename_2026_10_31, 0, Partial helper renames left aes128_gcm and curve25519_smalllimb calling names they no longer define. Fixed and passing NIST and RFC 7748 vectors on Phase 1. Not yet built natively. The X25519 ladder is still not constant-time.
    native_to_i64_compound_receiver_2026_10_31, 0, On the pinned Phase 2 producer arr.len().to_i64() and compound-expression receivers return 0 for every non-zero input with no error. This broke SQLCipher key sessions and the AES key schedule. The SQLCipher read path is worked around. The form remains at about 500 sites.
    env_get_cocompiled_signature_collision_2026_10_31, 0, On the Phase 1 seed interpreter an env_get imported as text can return the result of the text? definition in system_env_core. secret_ref and the fresh fixture now use env_get_opt. Other callers remain exposed.
    seed_interpreter_zeroize_not_guaranteed_2026_10_31, 0, Interpreter arrays are copy-on-write so a callee wipe can report success while the owner keeps its bytes. Wipe guarantees are judged natively. Accepted limit of the bootstrap seed.
    native_tuple_array_local_text_provenance_2026-10-30, 0, "Implicit native tuple-array text locals lose text representation. Reproduced with admitted compiler SHA 9633bf0af8b70d5f0324a35b244b3d08a62cdbcd1f8a3cd2aff246620f572dbd; explicit local tuple/text annotations produced the expected URL result and 8/8 fixture checks. Compiler phase remains unknown; see doc/08_tracking/bug/native_tuple_array_local_text_provenance_2026-10-30.md."
    retained_manual_system_link_old_seed_abi_2026_10_25, 0, "Existing documented issue: Retained runtime ABI blocks normal system link. Original producer identities and failure evidence are recorded in doc/08_tracking/bug/p4_retained_manual_route_2026_10_25.md; registration does not claim a compiler repair or new execution result."
    phase2_runner_tuple_resource_projection_2026_10_28, 0, "Existing documented issue: Runner tuple extraction loses resource field offsets. Original producer identities and failure evidence are recorded in doc/08_tracking/bug/phase2_runner_tuple_resource_projection_2026_10_28.md; registration does not claim a compiler repair or new execution result."
    phase2_runner_indexed_group_accumulation_2026_10_28, 0, "Existing documented issue: Runner indexed group counter updates disappear. Original producer identities and failure evidence are recorded in doc/08_tracking/bug/phase2_runner_indexed_group_accumulation_2026_10_28.md; registration does not claim a compiler repair or new execution result."
    phase2_runner_empty_limit_classification_2026_10_28, 0, "Existing documented issue: Runner Result tuple match corrupts child fields. Original producer identities and failure evidence are recorded in doc/08_tracking/bug/phase2_runner_empty_limit_classification_2026_10_28.md; registration does not claim a compiler repair or new execution result."
    phase2_result_payload_native_crash_2026_10_26, 0, "Existing documented issue: Result structured payload crashes native build. Original producer identities and failure evidence are recorded in doc/08_tracking/bug/phase2_result_payload_native_crash_2026_10_26.md; registration does not claim a compiler repair or new execution result."
    phase2_resource_scope_shell_shadow_2026_10_28, 0, "Existing documented issue: Resource scope shell local resolves as function. Original producer identities and failure evidence are recorded in doc/08_tracking/bug/phase2_resource_scope_shell_shadow_2026_10_28.md; registration does not claim a compiler repair or new execution result."
    phase2_private_sffi_cross_owner_export_unresolved_2026-10-27, 0, "Existing documented issue: Private SFFI cross-owner exports remain unresolved. Original producer identities and failure evidence are recorded in doc/08_tracking/bug/phase2_private_sffi_cross_owner_export_unresolved_2026-10-27.md; registration does not claim a compiler repair or new execution result."
    option_generic_inner_collapses_below_named_base_2026_10_20, 0, "Existing documented issue: Option structured inner types lose generic payload. Original producer identities and failure evidence are recorded in doc/08_tracking/bug/option_generic_inner_collapses_below_named_base_2026-10-20.md; registration does not claim a compiler repair or new execution result."
    mono_generic_fn_value_arg_2026-10-27, 0, "Existing documented issue: Generic function value lacks enclosing type inference. Original producer identities and failure evidence are recorded in doc/08_tracking/bug/mono_generic_fn_value_arg_2026-10-27.md; registration does not claim a compiler repair or new execution result."
    BUG-GNU-PHASE2-HOST-ALIAS-LINK-20261027, 0, "Existing documented issue: GNU Phase2 retains unavailable host aliases. Original producer identities and failure evidence are recorded in doc/08_tracking/bug/gnu_phase2_host_alias_coff_link_2026_10_27.md; registration does not claim a compiler repair or new execution result."
    phase2_imported_history_record_fields_2026_10_27, 0, "Indexed imported McpT32HistoryItem fields return command text for result and request_id; declaring-owner tuple view passed 11 focused checks without repairing the compiler."
    native_array_range_slice_lowering_2026_10_26, 0, "Native producer rejects history[250..] during MIR lowering; typed suffix-copy workaround preserves history retention."
    devhub_secured_db_key_session_open_failure_2026_10_27, 0, Fresh secured DB ledger1 compiled successfully with pinned Phase2 but actual execution returned Err at direct key-session open before encrypted decode. Messenger database access remains an unresolved main-feature blocker; this is not an infrastructure exception.
    phase2_octal_permission_mode_lowering_2026_10_27, 0, "Pinned P2 octal-mode source produced read-only final and staging files. The staging file contained the correct replacement token and expiry, so this failure was not a cache parser failure. Decimal 384 is exactly mode0600 and decimal448 is mode0700."
    phase2_u8_accelerated_sha256_ffi_carrier_2026_10_27, 0, Native binary upload failed with an invalid array handle before any loopback request. The accelerated u8 SHA256 boundary is incompatible with this producer. The workaround copies octets by index into the established i64 SHA256 engine without changing the public byte contract.
    windows_core_http_client_unavailable_2026_10_27, 0, "The Windows core native HTTP branch explicitly returns unavailable. A shared real curl compatibility transport uses bounded execution, private mode384 header/body/response files, no redirects and no TLS bypass; request secrets are absent from argv. Applications retain configured public std interfaces."
    phase2_result_tuple_try_binding_metadata_2026_10_27, 0, "Explicit typed Ok and Err bindings preserve u64 and byte-array tuple payload metadata where native Result propagation did not. Related compiler Result tuple repairs are in source, but the pinned producer has not been rebuilt and the compatibility bindings remain."
    phase2_bounded_process_text_abi_2026_10_27, 0, The actual HTTP compatibility probe returned missing command although curl8.21.0 was installed. The existing bounded tuple runtime provider accepts explicit command pointer and UTF8 length; a source adapter can preserve that ABI without changing the compiler or provider.
    phase2_module_static_array_concat_initialization_2026_10_27, 0, "The compatibility flag catalogs retain literal typed arrays instead of executing array concatenation while initializing module statics. Their public values remain unchanged. This is narrower than ordinary function-local array concatenation, which remains supported by other focused checks."
    bug_database_roundtrip_drops_overwide_legacy_rows_2026_10_27, 0, "The canonical registry contains legacy rows with more fields than their declared table schema. The generic table parser and full save do not preserve every overwide legacy row payload, so a complete BugDatabase.save round trip can discard untouched records or fields. The domain append-only API serializes only new records and preserves the complete original body byte for byte apart from inserted canonical rows."
    phase2_crc32_i64_width_spill_2026_10_27, 0, A native append-only registry copy preserved all original payload bytes but wrote CRC header -2292158518 while independent unsigned zlib computed2002808778. The values differ by2^32. This proves a CRC width or ABI boundary discrepancy; the exact widening or complement cause is not isolated. Masking public i64 CRC outputs to their low32bits preserves the actual CRC register contract.
    stage3_hir_shard_workers_collide_on_mem_snapshot_file_2026_10_19, 0, "run_ledger_shards spawns 8 HIR workers with the parent env; mem_snapshot_begin opens SIMPLE_MEM_SNAPSHOT_FILE O_EXCL, so every worker failed 'SIMPLE_MEM_SNAPSHOT_FILE could not be established safely', hir_shard_guard_block blocked the ledger and the next claim reported 'HIR shard ledger claim failed'. Fix: guard the retained-path mem_snapshot_begin with 'if not hir_shard_mode:' exactly like the streaming path."
    test_coverage_wrapper_native_build_refused_by_scv_admission_2026_10_19, 0, "`simple test <dir> --coverage` (seed bin/simple, release_phase3 01ff68b9c2c) builds the instrumented wrapper with `native-build --backend llvm --refresh-source-authority --entry-closure --runtime-bundle core-c-bootstrap`, and that build is refused before codegen, so every spec ABORTS BEFORE EXECUTION and the report is empty (Files tracked: 0). The rt_secure_temp_dir_set_parent twin is no longer the blocker. Fresh worktree: `SCV-E-ADMISSION: compile-event-journal-missing`; with SIMPLE_SCV_INVENTORY_COLD_INIT=1: `SCV-E-ADMISSION: git-event-refresh-failed` (inventory_events.spl _compiler_inventory_refresh_locked_v1; which `return nil` in _compiler_inventory_git_events_traced_v1 fires is not yet isolated; enabling SIMPLE_INVENTORY_TRACE_ATTEMPT instead fails with `semantic: invalid assignment: field assignment target is not a place`, i.e. the trace hook itself does not run on the seed). The warm main checkout also aborts (1.7s) with its real cause hidden behind a lint warning line; the diagnostic picker was fixed in the same change so the next run names it. The wrapper stages under test/native-generated--*/ (not gitignored, inside the SCV test family). Single-file mode is separate and also gives no report: `simple test <file>.spl --coverage` exits 0 with NO coverage output (the flag is silently ignored; test_runner_single gates on SIMPLE_COVERAGE only), and with SIMPLE_COVERAGE=1 it fails `error: spawned test process did not publish a valid child APK activation receipt`. UPDATE 2026-10-20 (work/cover-headers-and-coverage): root-cause chain, layer by layer. (1) compile-event-journal-missing: FIXED -- the coverage runner (lib test_runner_execute.spl coverage_scv_cold_init_needed) gives the FIRST wrapper build of a run SIMPLE_SCV_INVENTORY_COLD_INIT=1 only when build/scv has no journal pointer; later builds stay warm and strict. Verified: build/scv/source-inventory published from a fresh checkout. (2) git-event-refresh-failed under cold init was really the seed failing extern `__errno_location` (inventory_aliases.compiler_alias_present_v1 -> path_identity.path_entry_present): native_loader ProcessSymbolProvider/ChainedProvider stripped one leading `_` (Mach-O ABI) BEFORE lookup, so `__errno_location` was looked up as `_errno_location`, the JIT spliced the call to the interpreter, which has no backing. FIXED in source (exact name first, stripped spelling as fallback; native_loader unit tests red->green); takes effect only after a seed rebuild+redeploy -- the deployed bin/simple still has the bug. (3) REMAINING, not coverage-specific: with a private fixed seed the wrapper compile is killed by the unit-test resource-class default budget after ~20s (passes the budget with --no-limits), and then native-build --entry-closure fails in HIR shard workers with `semantic: type mismatch: cannot cast object to i64` -- a hello-world entry fails identically, so native-build of an entry closure on the seed is broken in general. Files tracked > 0 is blocked on that. (4) single-file `test <file>.spl --coverage` now exits 2 with `--coverage needs a directory target` instead of silently ignoring the flag (light-daemon client lane)."
    bdd_assert_outside_it_silent_false_green_2026_10_19, 0, "Seed dispatches assert_*/fail* as BDD builtins at Priority 3 (interpreter_call/mod.rs:723, bdd.rs eval_bdd_builtin) before user functions; a failure only sets BDD_EXPECT_FAILED, which is read solely at `it` end, so outside any `it` (comment doctest composites, `simple run` scripts, describe-level or before_all bodies) a wrong assert_equal exited 0 and `test x.spl --spl-doctest` reported 1 passed. `use std.spec.*` cannot help: the builtin shadows spec.spl assert_equal. FIXED for assert_*/fail* 2026-10-19: record_assertion_failure returns a hard error when BDD_INSIDE_IT is false. FIXED 2026-10-19 (same class, work/test-runner-leftovers): (1) `expect(2).to_equal(5)` at top level still exits 0 (matcher path, interpreter_method/mod.rs) -- now finish_bdd_matcher() (bdd.rs) makes a failed matcher outside an `it` a hard error, negated forms included; (2) pure-Simple: spec.spl fail_assertion outside a case pushes to current_test_errors with no consumer unless aggregate mode is active, so the self-hosted binary would false-green a `use std.spec.*` doctest too (the lib twin doctest_runner.spl build_spl_doctest_code injects that prelude; the app twin does not) -- now fatal: spec.spl tracks _case_depth around each example and fail_assertion exits 1 outside a case when aggregate mode is off. Remaining: a bare `expect <falsy>` (provisional, no matcher) outside an `it` is still not fatal. Not the unregistered-extern class and not name-resolution leniency."
    io_facade_exports_undeclared_time_now_unix_micros_2026_10_19, 0, "r13 stage2-admitted compiler (sha e6cb4bfd55..), native-build --backend llvm --entry-closure src/app/devhub/main.spl on release_phase3 12be79bd73b: hir-reexport-chase-unresolved facade=lib.nogc_async_mut.io item=time_now_unix_micros, then hir-fatal 'module std.io has no exported item time_now_unix_micros' at src/app/devhub/cmd_daily_debug.spl:24. io.spl line 146 exports the name with no declaring import (comment says delegated via wildcard from std.nogc_async_mut.io.*); io/__init__.spl does export it. The seed interpreter accepts the same import (devhub --help rc=0). 492 of 493 HIR modules lowered; build exit 1 after 353s, 2.1 GB RSS."
    native_parser_nested_quotes_in_interpolation_2026_10_19, 0, "Same compiler, entry src/app/llm_caret/main.spl: 'parse error in src/lib/gc_async_mut/gpu/browser_engine/net/h1_client.spl: 649:69: expected ), got StringLit' on the expression h1_decode_content_encoding(framed, interpolated text containing encoding ?? two-double-quotes). The Rust seed parses it. Per CLAUDE.md fix the parser rather than rewriting the call site silently. Build exit 1 after 103s, 2.7 GB RSS."
    native_mir_lambda_and_enum_eq_block_caret_cs_2026_10_19, 0, "Same compiler, entry src/app/llm_caret/cs_main.spl reaches MIR then fails: E-MIR-EXPR-Lambda x21 (nogc_async_mut/io/buffer.spl 130,155,166,275,288,301,320,333), operator overload not found for enum-like types compared with == (RtHalOperationKind x12, RtHalProviderKind x9, FileMode x6, EnvAccessKind x6, Encoding x4), unresolved method close x7 and is_open x8 (nogc_sync_mut and nogc_async_mut io/buffer.spl). Build exit 1 after 277s, 3.4 GB RSS."
    interp_option_unwrapped_text_starts_with_nil_2026_10_19, 0, "Repro (seed rc.1 testrun_seed3 and deployed bin/simple beta.14, interpreter): fn opt(s: text) -> text? returning Some(s); val bv = opt('/h/s/tmp')!; bv.starts_with('/h/s/') and bv.ends_with('tmp') evaluate to nil, (opt(x) ?? 'd').starts_with(..) also nil; bv.contains(..) and bv == .. are correct; a literal receiver is correct. Effect: is_strict_storage_descendant compares canonical_candidate! with starts_with and always answers false, so validate_storage_containment returns OutsideRoot and tooling_workspace_path fails for every worktree (probed in /home/yoon/dev/simple and the release_phase3 worktree). MCP caret_mail_list, caret_storage_ls and caret_wiki_search all answer 'centralized worktree storage is unavailable' (main_lazy_caret_tools.spl _write_input). The caret tool CLI itself (src/app/llm_caret/tool_cli.spl) runs fine when invoked directly. Native MCP server shows the same symptom; whether native codegen shares the same root cause is unverified. Do not work around in path_policy; fix method dispatch on unwrapped Option receivers."
    devhub_redaction_comma_secret_suffix_leak_2026_10_19, 0, "redact_devhub_diagnostic('token: <dq>alpha,beta<dq>') returns 'token: ***,beta<dq>' (spec expects 'token: ***'); 'Set-Cookie: session=one, refresh=two' returns 'Set-Cookie: ***, refresh=two'. _redact_sensitive_assignment ends the masked span at the first comma with no quote or cookie-header awareness. Failing: redaction_comma_spec (1/1), redaction_followup_spec (1/7). Security-relevant: secret material reaches diagnostics."
    devhub_email_contract_drift_2026_10_19, 0, "Seed testrun 2026-10-19 on release_phase3 12be79bd73b: email_cmd_spec 3 fail (provider parsed as outlook where spec expects outlook_imap; handle_email returns 2 where spec expects 1 for actionable errors; inbox via mail-cli evidence failed), email_smoke_spec 1 fail (unknown subcommand returns 2, spec 1), email_shared_config_spec 1 fail (malformed shared config raises array index out of bounds index 0 length 0 instead of a rejection). Owner must decide whether the code or the specs hold the contract."
    app_launchers_no_admitted_runtime_aarch64_linux_2026_10_19, 0, "Candidate lists in bin/devhub, bin/caret, bin/itf, bin/dash, bin/portal, bin/sj and bin/simple-interp include x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu but not aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu, and simple_runtime_provenance_admits rejects the Rust seed even when passed as SIMPLE_BINARY. On this aarch64 host bin/devhub --help and bin/caret --help exit 127 'no Simple runtime found' in the main clone and the worktree. Causes 17 devhub system-spec failures (devhub_terminal_ui_spec 7/10, gh_shim_backend_routing_spec 10/12). Adding the path alone flips nothing until an admitted pure-Simple runtime is deployed for aarch64."
    llm_caret_unit_specs_rotted_2026_10_19, 0, "openai_api_spec and claude_api_spec open a docstring on line 2 that is never closed (Unterminated triple-quoted string); retry_spec fails to parse (expected expression, found Indent); claude_full/ink/terminal_querier_spec fails to parse (found RParen). claude_cli_spec duplicates its use lines, defines _LB/_RB but calls undefined _Q and _escape_json (27 failures, function _Q not found). Same seed parses the rest of the 97-file directory, so these look like merge damage, not parser gaps; confirm against a pure-Simple parser before repairing."
    seed_coalesce_stateful_operand_twice_2026_10_12, 0, "Seed lowering of `stream.finish_hex()` coalesced to an empty-text default evaluates the stateful finish twice; the second call returns nil, so the digest is lost. Caller workaround binds the result before coalescing (release_phase3 workaround 0f7368cd97d, recover fcc1d91ea1b). Compiler repair pending; qualified DB reconciliation pending."
    pure_simple_nested_extern_registration_2026_10_12, 0, "A function-nested `extern fn rt_cpu_count` is not registered by the pure-Simple compiler. Workaround hoists it to module scope (release_phase3 workaround 657ca5c5fb5, recover 0f7368cd97d). Compiler repair pending; qualified DB reconciliation pending."
    llvm_inline_asm_dialect_false_green_2026_10_12, 0, "Intel-syntax port in/out inline asm is dropped by the LLVM seed path without a dialect switch. Workaround wraps each instruction in .intel_syntax/.att_syntax (release_phase3 workaround ef00661e2e3, recover 5c225cff453). Compiler repair pending; qualified DB reconciliation pending."
    item5_phase3_early_mir_crash_2026_10_14, 0, "Frozen b061/a713 canonical381 closure exited139 after635.226s. HIR381 completed; Mono65 functions430 calls124 specializations and zero unresolved. MIR0/381 then crash; no objects. Memory reserve remained above21GiB. Corrected GDB captured SIGSEGV at PC0xb90168 in MirLowering.relocate_provider_type+244, called by relocate_provider_default then register_provider_class. The invalid provider-type operand cause remains under repair; the CompileError warning is not established as causal."
    item5_generic_optional_payload_acceptance_2026_10_14, 0, "Actual wrap_unknown<text> specialization compiled an UnknownEnvelope.Value(Some(value)) for declared i64? payload. Reachable ELF specialization verified; no negative execution or passing rejection claimed. Exact post-substitution validation boundary remains unresolved. Primitive positives and wrong-inner/Any rejection results do not qualify this generic case."
    item5_cranelift_module_data_support_2026_10_14, 0, "Actual AOT rejects imported globals and signal handler non-scalar initialization. Guards remain intact. LLVM object generation passes for signal_stubs, trace_policy, AST nodes and process_ops. Mixed LLVM/Cranelift linkage and runtime initialization are not qualified."
    item5_native_object_resource_growth_2026_10_14, 0, "SymbolTable87 passed MIR then exited143 at shared4GiB RAM-plus-swap reserve;69 private LLVM objects retained. Aggregate process RSS exceeded28GiB in some successful cohorts; shared-memory contribution is unisolated. No memory-leak cause or performance qualification claimed. Owned temporary swap is diagnostic only."
    item5_native_build_threads_ineffective_2026_10_14, 0, "Actual pure-Simple native builder reports thread counts above one have no effect; module generation remains sequential. Separate diagnostic object jobs and parallel repair agents do not prove internal backend parallelism. Parallel implementation and qualification remain pending."
    item5_backend_error_opaque_enum_2026_10_14, 0, "Retained AOT message renders CompileFailed as opaque enum address. Actual backend messages identify missing static-data support. Private36945ca diagnostic patch retains typed CompileError fields and explicit authority variants; patch is unbuilt and unlanded."
    explicit_generic_interpolation_transport_2026_10_14, 0, "Canonical six profile calls lost flat/rich/HIR type arguments before the rich bridge. Computing typed helper vals inside the same receipt branch preserves all six argument arrays and clears canonical monomorphization. Underlying interpolation owner remains unresolved; workaround is not a parser repair."
    bare_enum_pattern_binding_in_compiler_2026_10_14, 0, "Actual SymbolTable.is_function HIR lowered bare Function to Binding and wildcard, causing B5b. Qualified SymbolKind.Function workaround clears B5b and reaches backend generation. General contested bare enum resolution remains open."
    mir_json_c0_escaping_2026_10_12, 0, "MIR JSON forwards C0 controls other than LF CR TAB; old strlen joins may hide NUL loss while target counted joins preserve invalid raw bytes. Minimal C0 and whole-Unicode repair plus32-control native decoder fixture AUTHORED_UNEXECUTED. OPEN."
    imported_generic_native_callee_owner_loss_2026_10_12, 0, "Earlier ordinary imported native names passed on qualified predecessor. Current archive signature preserves linkage metadata with v2 digest; exact source-containing producer blocked during discovery. Generic extern/linkage modes/full core gates remain open."
    nul_literal_double_box_constructor_2026_10_12, 0, "Actual d356 native literal emits new_literal then raw new with tagged operand; GDB proves RTS header copied before helper. Byte-only native probe compile and strict link pass but run1. NUL-only Ptr(U8) constructor operand/signature candidate and frontend-MIR assertions authored; changed producer execution unqualified. OPEN."
    runtime_byte_text_utf8_invariant_2026_10_12, 0, "Packed and boxed bytes bypassed UTF-8 validation before RuntimeString construction. A separate legacy array-length shortcut also admitted NIL/scalar zero as empty arrays. Repairs normalize malformed bytes and explicitly reject nonheap/nullheap receivers; actual runtime tests remain unexecuted."
    archive_owner_source_grammar_2026_10_12, 0, "Two malformed multiline else spellings and reserved pass local prevent current-source compiler discovery. Minimal reviewed source corrections passed actual discovery; native/compiler/core gates remain open. No general parser repair claimed."
    block_error_span_source_metadata_loss_2026_10_12, 0, "Current error_at/error_span replace payload source file with empty text. Preserve payload.file; exact recovered-seed owner native fixture passed eight assertions. Latest upstream already fixes tuple annotation/imports/length; not duplicated. Full self-host checks and persisted SSpec remain UNEXECUTED; draft source qualification OPEN."
    block_highlighting_raw_escape_native_hex_2026_10_12, 0, "Native focused bootstrap diagnostic exposed unavailable str.is_hex_digit and raw single-quoted newline/backslash comparisons. Frozen candidate has seven distinct native cases PASS across three bounded cycles; final latest-source narrow integration is UNEXECUTED. Preserve concurrent keyword/helper/optional repair. Full Stage2 and non-Linux qualification remain OPEN."
    result_err_missing_native_projection_2026_10_12, 0, "Focused native repair passed 18 assertions plus two fail-closed compiler cases and expected None unwrap panic; full repository verification remains open."
    enum_payload_declaring_owner_binding_2026_10_12, 0, "Focused native verification_codegen_types HIR failure repaired by b20ad174 successor; payload terminal registered without enum-owner alias. Full aggregate and standalone semantic spec remain unqualified."
    windows_terminal_raw_bytes_crlf_translation_2026_10_12, 0, "Actual retained Simple terminal strict link succeeds and run exits zero, but Windows CRT expands source LF to CRLF: 20 input bytes return20 yet21 stdout bytes. Canonical raw text provider fwrite owner defect; source-only Windows FILE-associated handle proposal and new fixtures UNEXECUTED. Prior feature3 STOP preserved."
    windows_piped_process_cold_handle_growth_2026_10_12, 0, "ActualWindows process primitive fixture fails final handle equality code36 in cycles2and3. Finaldiagnostic baseline128,emptyargv131,cancel158,threads158,slots158,final158; Unicodephase missing. Ownerattribution OPEN; no per-process leak or legitimatewarmcache claim. 3STOP,no fourthretry."
    process_stdout_result_eof_drain_race_2026_10_12, 0, "Source-confirmed stdout EOF/liveness race. Coordinated Linux POSIX owner cycle1 PASS with real children and OS fault injection; native SPL facade, public RuntimeValue spawn, other OS and core gates remain UNEXECUTED. Bug OPEN."
